Fortran 77 Tutorial -- adapted and extended edition
====================================================

This repository contains an adapted and extended edition of the Fortran 77
tutorial written at Stanford University by Erik Boman, Sarah T. Whitlock and
Paul H. Hargrove:

    https://web.stanford.edu/class/me200c/tutorial_77/

It is NOT an official version of that tutorial, and it has not been reviewed
or endorsed by its authors or by Stanford University.

The repository contains material under two different terms.

1. Material from the original tutorial
--------------------------------------

The parts taken from the original tutorial (text and example programs) are

    Copyright (c) 1995-7 by Stanford University. All rights reserved.

and are used under the permission granted in its preface:

    "Permission to use this tutorial for educational and other
    non-commercial purposes is granted provided all author and copyright
    information is retained."

Any use of these parts must respect that permission: educational or other
non-commercial purposes only, retaining all author and copyright information.

2. New material of this edition
-------------------------------

Everything else -- the new and rewritten text, the exercises and their
solutions, the code added to complete the example programs, the test
scripts and the documentation -- is

    Copyright (c) 2026 Roberto Augusto Gómez Loenzo

and is licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-
ShareAlike 4.0 International License (CC BY-NC-SA 4.0). The full text is in
LICENSE-CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt, and a summary is available at

    https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/

In short: you may copy, redistribute and adapt this material for
non-commercial purposes, provided that you credit both the original authors
(Erik Boman, Sarah T. Whitlock, Paul H. Hargrove, Stanford University) and
the adapter (Roberto Augusto Gómez Loenzo), indicate if changes were made,
and distribute your adaptations under the same license.

See also "A note on this edition" in the preface of the tutorial
(tutorial.pdf), which lists the main changes with respect to the original.
